Import meshes from the user's local Blender into Studio as a Model in Workspace. Each object becomes a MeshPart (modifiers applied, triangulated) that keeps its material's Base Color image texture, or else its plain Base Color. Meshes and textures upload as assets owned by the Studio user. Re-importing the same group updates that Model in place and skips unchanged meshes and textures. With position, the Model's bottom center lands exactly there, turned by rotation. Without it, a new Model appears in front of the camera. The reply includes the Model's size and bottomCenter. Imports `collection`, else `objects`, else the Blender selection, else all visible meshes. Keep each mesh under ~20k triangles. Costs 0.5 Ropilot Actions. Afterwards, check the result with ropilot_studio_screenshot focused on the Model.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__ropilot__ropilot_blender_import(args: {
  // Blender collection to import, with all its visible meshes in their relative layout
  collection?: string;
  // Model name in Workspace (default: collection or object name)
  name?: string;
  // Blender object names to import
  objects?: Array<string>;
  // [x, y, z] in studs for the Model's bottom center
  position?: Array<number>;
  // Degrees to turn the Model around the vertical axis. Models built facing Blender -Y face +Z in Roblox.
  rotation?: number;
  // Studs per Blender unit (default 1)
  scale?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

