Import the animation on an armature from ropilot_blender_import_rig into Studio. Bakes scene.frame_start through frame_end into a KeyframeSequence, publishes it as an Animation asset owned by the Studio user, and creates an Animation instance with that AnimationId (load it with Animator:LoadAnimation). Pass the same rig as ropilot_blender_import_rig, or omit it for the standard R15 dummy. For the dummy, the KeyframeSequence goes to ServerStorage.RopilotAnimations and the Animation to ReplicatedStorage.Animations. For a custom rig, both go in the rig (AnimSaves). If publishing fails, the KeyframeSequence is still saved and the reply says why. Costs 0.5 Ropilot Actions.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__ropilot__ropilot_blender_import_animation(args: {
  // Armature object in Blender, from ropilot_blender_import_rig
  armature: string;
  // Loop the animation, for idles, walks, and runs (default false)
  loop?: boolean;
  // Animation name, e.g. 'Wave' (default 'Animation'). Replaces an earlier one with this name.
  name?: string;
  // Animation priority (default Action)
  priority?: "Core" | "Idle" | "Movement" | "Action" | "Action2" | "Action3" | "Action4";
  // Publish as an Animation asset (default true). false only saves the KeyframeSequence.
  publish?: boolean;
  // Path of the custom rig Model the animation is for. Omit for the standard R15 dummy.
  rig?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

